\subsection*{Ethics statement}
This is a theoretical and methodological study of self-supervised training dynamics on synthetic data and the public CIFAR-10 dataset~\citep{krizhevsky2009cifar}; it involves no human subjects, personal data or deployed system, and we are not aware of an ethical concern specific to it.

\subsection*{Reproducibility statement}
Assumptions are stated with each result in \cref{sec:theory,sec:ext} and complete proofs and derivations are in \cref{app:proofs,app:ext}.
\Cref{app:details} gives the statistics, initialisation, optimiser, step sizes, horizons, rank threshold, grids and compute of every experiment.
The supplementary material contains the code, the per-run results, the pre-registration files and the scripts that regenerate every figure, table and quoted number (each number in the text is generated from a named result file), with the commands in \texttt{code/README.md}; the linear experiments need no external data.

\subsection*{AI use statement}
In this work, we used generative AI tools for all tasks with required disclosure: research ideas, formulating claims and proofs, methodology and experiment design, implementing methods, running experiments and interpreting results; generating synthetic data is not applicable beyond the simulated inputs of the linear experiments, which our code generates.
Additionally, we used generative AI tools for drafting the text, producing the figures and tables, writing code and searching the literature.
The work was carried out by a team of large-language-model agents with separate roles (study planning, literature review, theory and experiments, figures, writing, venue conformance and independent internal review); every proof was checked against numerical solutions of the dynamics, every number in the text is generated by code from the result files, every citation was checked against its bibliographic record and first-publication date, and the internal reviewer recompiled the paper and re-checked its numbers against the results.
All AI-assisted work was reviewed in this way, by the internal-review agent and against the code and result files; we take responsibility for the final content of this work, including text, claims or artifacts produced with the aid of generative AI.
